	<key>readme</key>
	<string># kafka-docker-playground (kdp)

Keyword **kdp** (the first line says what is running, 🆕 when the clone has a newer workflow), or the Universal Action **kdp: config, stack trace, connector class, key, case…** on selected text: a connector config gets validate / convert / repro bootstrap, a stack trace `analyze logs`, a connector class its plugin and examples, a config key `kdp key`.

| Query | What |
| --- | --- |
| `kdp find &lt;words&gt;` | `playground find-example`: examples (and repro models) |
| `kdp history [words]` | `playground history`: replay a run |
| `kdp plugin &lt;words&gt; [version]` | pick the plugin in the list (↩ fills it in), then a version in its list, then connector-plugin info / changelog / sourcecode / dependencies / cve-scan |
| `kdp key &lt;words&gt;` | pick the key in the list, then a connector that has it: connector-plugin config-key (`--since-version` with a connector) |
| `kdp docs [words]` | deep dive and toolkit pages on kafka-docker-playground.io |
| `kdp connector [words]` | pick a running connector (failed first), then diagnose, status, tasks, metrics, history, config, offsets, topics, restart failed tasks, pause / resume |
| `kdp logs [container] [pattern]` | pick a container, then its errors, last lines, the lines matching a pattern, or follow them in the terminal |
| `kdp topic [words]` | pick a topic: describe, number of records, last / first records, grep, DLQ inspect |
| `kdp schema [words]` | pick a subject: describe, latest schema, history, diff, compatibility |
| `kdp ci [words]` | pick a CI test: get-ci-result (with logs and HTML report), 🔥 issues |
| `kdp status` | playground status, connector status / diagnose, connect errors, broker health |
| `kdp repro [words]` | reproduction models, mine first (only when `reproduction-models/` has models) |
| `kdp notes [words]` | notes folder, resume the Claude Code session that wrote a note (only when the folder exists) |
| `kdp case &lt;number&gt;` (or `kdp &lt;number&gt;`) | ticket link (`ticket_url`), notes and repro models of the case |

Keys: ↩ copy the command (or open), ⌘ VS Code, ⌃ run in the terminal, ⌥ / ⇧ depend on the mode (hold the key to see the subtitle).
⌃ on an example runs `playground run`, which stops the environment that is running.

Read-only commands (`plugin`, `key`, `status`, the repro hand-off report) show their output in the Alfred window, streamed while they run (↩ runs it again, `watch` + ↩ every 5 s, text + ↩ filters the lines, ⇧↩ opens the HTML report, ⌘↩ copies the output, ⌥↩ the command), unless **Show output** says terminal. Interactive ones (`playground run`, `claude`) always go to the terminal.

Commands sent to the terminal go where the **Run in the terminal** setting says: the terminal set in Alfred Preferences &gt; Features &gt; Terminal (default), a new VS Code integrated terminal, Terminal.app, or the clipboard only.

Installed by `playground tools install-alfred-workflow` (source in scripts/alfred-workflow/ of kafka-docker-playground).
</string>
